$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Syntheses of Thioether Ligands.17 A reaction
mixture containing 2‐hydroxythiophenol (7.92 mmol) in 8 mL of dry DMF was
treated with KHCO3 (9.04 mmol) and bromide (7.92 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature in the required time. The mixture
was diluted with water, then extracted with Et2O (3×20 mL). The combined
organic phases were washed with water, dried with MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. Chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexane, 3:97)
give a colorless oil. 2-(Isopropylthio)phenol (HL-iPr). Yield 86%
(reaction in 3 h). ESI-MS: m/z = 167 [M-H]-; 1H NMR (300.1 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.47 (d, 1H), 7.30 (t, 1H), 7.02 (d, 1H), 6.90 (m, 2H), 3.12 (m, 1H),
1.28 (d, 6H).
